# Zero downloads (owner decision b). MSBuild reads this file for every build or restore started on a
# project or solution under app/. The bindings projects mark themselves IsAotCompatible/IsTrimmable,
# which makes the SDK fetch the trimming analyzer pack Microsoft.NET.ILLink.Tasks from their own
# (user-level) NuGet sources. The app does not trim or publish AOT, so it builds the bindings without
# those analyzers; the bindings' own solution and CI job keep them. The -restoreProperty copies are
# needed because "dotnet build" restores with -restoreProperty, which replaces the -property values.
-p:IsAotCompatible=false
-p:IsTrimmable=false
-p:NuGetAudit=false
-restoreProperty:IsAotCompatible=false
-restoreProperty:IsTrimmable=false
-restoreProperty:NuGetAudit=false
